$Id: README.gui,v 1.2 2011/10/30 23:53:59 drmiller Exp $

The GUI is java based. All the *.class files are required, and optional fonts
are desirable. All fonts are *.ttf and in the "fonts" subdirectory.

This does seem to build and run correctly on OSX as well as Linux (known to work
on Debian and RHEL).

Simplest build procedure is

	make install

which should build everything and install it in ~/wang700apc.
All the java is packaged into a jar file, along with fonts and icons.
The GUI may then be launched with the command:

	~/wang700apc/run

This creates a sub-process to run the simulator. Currently, you still need
the terminal window for the printer(s), and for any diagnostic output.
This means that if you want to setup an "Application Launcher" button
on your desktop or panel, you need to select the "in Terminal Window" option.

Note, "Run-Learn" mode (both Run and Learn buttons pushed together) works
using your native keyboard shift key. With either Run or Learn down,
press Shift and click the other.  both will be down and the alternate functions
of the special keys is available. Clicking, without Shift, on either button
will release the other.
